<Base title="About" subtitle="شازم (Shazim) means خوشی (khushi - happiness)">
  <p>
    For quite a while till my late teenage years, I didn't know what my name meant. Whenever my
    mother was asked what it meant she usually replied "Oh it was the name of a persian prince!". I
    have yet to find this persian prince, even AI can't. In the meantime, I can thank my sweet mom
    and grandfather, as well as the arabic and persian languages, for my unique name and its
    meaning.
  </p>

  <p>Do you know what your name means? Does it affect how you see yourself?</p>

  <hr />

  <p>
    My natural disposition is to speak in polymathematical abstracts, which has warranted many to
    call me a Philosopher. In the modern world however, a philosopher is rarely given a place
    anywhere. Currently I'm working as a <a href="/work"> Software Engineer at Xbox</a> hoping to apply
    human-centric principles to create experiences that not only give the user what's valuable to them
    but also what's joyful to them.
  </p>

  <p>
    I am ever in pursuit of that ikigai work path, that uses my talents and passions most
    beneficially.
  </p>
</Base>
